{"answer": "Spain: the rent can be updated only on each anniversary of the contract, in the terms the parties agreed, and without an express agreement no update applies [1]. The increase from the annual update cannot exceed the percentage variation of the consumer price index at the date of each update [1]. The updated rent is due from the month after the party notifies the other in writing, stating the percentage applied [1].

Colombia: after each twelve months of the contract at the same price, the rent may be increased by at most 100% of the increase in the consumer price index in the previous calendar year, within the cap of art. 18 [2]. The update applies only with the landlord's notice of the amount and the date it takes effect [2].

Dubai: before a lease expires, the parties may amend its terms or reconsider the rent [3]. Failing agreement, the Tribunal may determine the fair rent [3]. A party who wants to amend a term must notify the other no less than ninety days before the lease expires, unless otherwise agreed [4].", "change": "none: I made no substantive change and kept every condition, number and exception the reference gives."}
